-- Bandito Arms weapons and the western body armour line, Rifts New West.
-- Printed 173-181. Fifteen new rows: eight guns and seven suits.
--
-- One-off data script, run once per environment. NOT a migration - it adds
-- rows, not schema.
--
--   node scripts/d1-apply.mjs --local apps/character-creator/db/add-new-west-gear-a-bandito.sql
--
-- EVERY NUMBER HERE WAS READ OFF A RENDER, not off the OCR cache. This book
-- sets its weapon entries in BOXED PANELS that break the cache's column
-- analysis, and the failure is silent: on printed 173 the Bandit IP-10's
-- "Cost: 12,000 credits" is separated from its own stat block by an unrelated
-- "Black Market Prices for E-Clips" sidebar, and on printed 180 a block of
-- four illustration captions sits between the NG Range Rider's M.D.C. and its
-- price. Nothing about either page looks wrong in the cache. This is the same
-- two-column fault already recorded three times in this book for class skill
-- lists (Highwayman printed 86, Wired Gunslinger 109, Professional Gambler
-- 119) - see docs/surveys/new-west.md.
--
-- THE CACHE ALSO MIS-SETS TWO STRINGS THE RENDER SETTLES:
--   * "MI 'Vaqueros' Armor" reads as "Ml Vaqueros" in the text layer. MI is
--     the Manistique Imperium, which the entry names in its own first line.
--   * the Bandit 6000's cost prints as "80,000-100.000" - a period where a
--     comma belongs. Stored as 80,000 to 100,000.
--
-- THREE OF THIS SECTION'S SUITS ARE ALREADY IN THE CATALOG AND ARE NOT
-- DUPLICATED. The Black Market sells knock-offs of the old CS armour, and the
-- book says outright they are "identical to the old CS body armor in every
-- way, except the standard colors". Those rows exist from RUE:
--   * CA-1 Heavy Dead Boy Armor (ca-1-heavy-dead-boy-armor) - 18 lbs, main
--     body 80, helmet 50, arms 35, legs 50. New West prints the same five
--     figures.
--   * CA-2 Light Dead Boy Armor (ca-2-light-dead-boy-armor) - 9 lbs, main
--     body 50. New West agrees on weight and main body and prints ONE M.D.C.
--     block for both suits, so its helmet/arms/legs figures are the HEAVY
--     suit's; RUE states the light suit's separately (35/15/24) and is the
--     fuller reading.
--   * Dog Pack DPM Riot Armor (dog-pack-dpm-riot-armor) - 8 lbs, main body
--     30, arms 10, legs 20. New West prints 10 lbs and a light/heavy split
--     (main body 35 or 50, arms 10+3, legs 15+5) that RUE does not have.
-- What differs is the PRICE, because these are Black Market goods rather than
-- CS issue: light Dead Boy 40,000 and heavy 50,000 against RUE's 35,000, and
-- Dog Pack light 12,000 and heavy 18,000 against a row that carries no cost at
-- all. The gear table holds one cost per row, so recording New West's figures
-- would mean either overwriting RUE's or creating a second row with identical
-- stats. NEITHER IS DONE HERE - it is a catalog-shape question, filed for
-- decision rather than settled by an import.
--
-- MDC HOLDS THE MAIN BODY, per the convention the Triax and Free Quebec gear
-- scripts set; the per-location breakdown is in the description.
--
-- THE CAVALRY BARDING IS ARMOUR, NOT A VESSEL. It is a suit worn BY a horse -
-- the book files it in the body armour section and prices it like one - so it
-- lands in gear alongside the human suits rather than in vehicles with the
-- robot horses.

INSERT OR IGNORE INTO gear (slug, name, system, category, weight_lbs, cost, cost_note, damage, is_mega_damage, range, payload, rate_of_fire, ar, sdc, mdc, description, source_book) VALUES
('bandit-ip-10-ion-pistol', 'Bandit IP-10 Ion Pistol', 'rifts', 'weapon', 3, 12000, '12,000 credits', '3D6 M.D.', 1, '400 feet (122 m)', '10 shots from a standard short E-Clip, 20 shots with a long E-Clip', 'Standard', NULL, NULL, NULL, 'Also known as the "Eye-Pie Ten". Bandito Arms built it for shooters who wanted heavy damage out of a sidearm; the range is relatively short but the damage is impressive. It is styled to look like a revolver of the Old West, with the E-Clip designed to fit into the handle. Bonuses: well balanced, +1 to strike.', 'Rifts World Book 14: New West p.173'),
('bandit-lp1-laser-pistol', 'Bandit LP1 Laser Pistol', 'rifts', 'weapon', 2, 20000, '20,000 credits for the gun, 2000 credits per magazine', '2D4 M.D. (or 1D8 if one prefers)', 1, '1000 feet (305 m)', '20 shots from a standard short E-Clip, 40 shots with a long E-Clip', 'Standard', NULL, NULL, NULL, 'Also known as the "No Lip" pistol. A lightweight, highly accurate laser pistol with good range. The damage yield could be higher, but the accuracy and the large payload more than offset it. Bonuses: superior laser focusing optics, light weight and handling give +1 to strike.', 'Rifts World Book 14: New West p.173'),
('bandit-bigbore-revolver', 'Bandit BigBore Revolver', 'rifts', 'weapon', 4, 6500, '6,500 credits for the gun, 80 credits per round or 10,000 credits for a gross (box of 144 rounds)', '1D6 M.D. per round', 1, '200 feet (91 m)', 'Six; revolver style cylinder weapon', 'Single shot; each shot counts as a melee action unless shooting wild', NULL, NULL, NULL, 'Also known as the "BB-6", for six-shooter, and the first of the BigBore series - a line of old style S.D.C. guns firing heavy explosive rounds that has been met with wild enthusiasm among gunfighters and bandits. The "bullets" could be considered small grenades. Horror Factor 10 when pointed in someone''s face. A P.S. of 14 is required to shoot it (a weaker P.S. is -2 to strike even on an aimed shot and -6 shooting wild) and a P.S. of 17 to fire it one handed. KNOCK DOWN: humans and human-sized D-bees who are shot must roll a 20 sided die equal to or above the attacker''s strike roll to keep their footing. Success means the character feels kicked by a mule but stands, suffering no penalty except the loss of initiative. Failure knocks the victim off his feet and back 1D4 feet, losing initiative and one melee attack. Characters in M.D.C. body armour are knocked down too; those in power armour, full conversion cyborgs, robots, giants, supernatural beings and creatures of magic are not.', 'Rifts World Book 14: New West p.174'),
('bandit-bigbore-sawed-off', 'Bandit BigBore Sawed-Off', 'rifts', 'weapon', 6, 15000, '15,000 credits for the gun, 120 credits per round or 16,000 credits for a gross (box of 144 rounds)', '2D4 M.D. per single round or 4D4 M.D. per double-barrel blast', 1, '150 feet (46 m)', 'Two, or 12 with an ammo drum', 'Each shot, single or double barrel, counts as one melee action', NULL, NULL, NULL, 'Also known as the "BB Sawed-Off" and the "Mule", which is what it kicks like. It looks like a sawed-off shotgun and fires a large, high explosive shell with even greater knock down power than the BB-6. Horror Factor 12 against most mortal opponents. A P.S. of 18 is required to shoot it (less is knocked on their butt and loses one melee attack) and 22 to fire it one handed. Single barrel and double-barrelled varieties are available; the double-barrel is most popular. KNOCK DOWN: the target rolls a 20 sided die at -6 to stay standing, needing to equal or surpass the attacker''s strike roll. Success leaves the character staggered, knocked to his knees and without initiative. Failure flings the victim 8-10 feet (2.4 to 3 m) before he hits the ground, losing initiative, losing one melee attack, and momentarily dazed - all combat bonuses halved for one melee round per blast endured. Characters in M.D.C. body armour suffer the same. Those in power armour, full conversion cyborgs, robots, giants, supernatural beings and creatures of magic get +6 to save against knock down, but still lose initiative and are staggered by each shot.', 'Rifts World Book 14: New West p.174-175'),
('bandit-bigbore-shotgun', 'Bandit BigBore Shotgun', 'rifts', 'weapon', 8, 18000, '18,000 credits for the gun, 120 credits per round or 16,000 credits for a gross (box of 144 rounds)', '2D4 M.D. per single round or 4D4 M.D. per double-barrel blast', 1, '300 feet (122 m)', 'Four, or 12 with an ammo clip', 'Each shot, single or double barrel, counts as one melee action', NULL, NULL, NULL, 'Also known as the "BB Long-Barrel". It looks like a heavy shotgun and fires the same high explosive shell as the BB Sawed-Off, with the same knock down effect; its advantage is the greater range. Horror Factor 12. A P.S. of 18 is required to shoot it (less is knocked off their feet and loses one melee attack) and 22 to fire it one handed. Single barrel and double-barrelled varieties are available.', 'Rifts World Book 14: New West p.175'),
('bandit-5000-bigbore-rail-gun', 'Bandit 5000 BigBore Rail Gun', 'rifts', 'weapon', 25, 50000, '50,000 to 55,000 credits for the gun, 80 credits per round or 10,000 credits for a gross (box of 144 rounds)', '1D6 M.D. per single round or 2D6 M.D. per short burst of six rounds', 1, '2000 feet (610 m); the E-Clip provides the extra "zip"', 'Standard drum: 60 rounds or 10 bursts. A large backpack ammo drum holding 240 rounds (40 bursts) can be substituted, weighing an additional 22 pounds (10 kg). The E-Clip fires 960 rounds (160 bursts) before it needs replacing.', 'One at a time or in bursts; each counts as one melee action, but the burst is less controlled and less accurate', NULL, NULL, NULL, 'Also known as the "Big Bear", and the first of the Black Market light rail guns - man-portable weapons light enough for a single soldier with a P.S. of 20 to use comfortably while still delivering the firepower of a rail gun. The basic design was uncovered by Bandito Arms at Area 51. The weight includes an E-Clip and a standard 60 round ammunition drum. Reloading takes one melee round (15 seconds), or 30 without the W.P. heavy weapons skill. A P.S. of 20 or higher is needed to use it without penalty, otherwise -3 to strike. Same knock down as the sawed-off BB-Mule. Bonuses: laser targeting standard, +1 to strike on aimed shots.', 'Rifts World Book 14: New West p.175-176'),
('bandit-5500-flechette-rail-gun', 'Bandit 5500 Flechette Rail Gun', 'rifts', 'weapon', 30, 52000, '52,000 to 58,000 credits for the gun, 80 credits per flechette round or 10,000 credits for a gross (box of 144 rounds)', '1D4 M.D. per single round or 3D6 M.D. per short burst of six rounds', 1, '2000 feet (610 m); the energy clip provides the extra "zip"', 'Standard drum: 42 rounds or 7 bursts. A large backpack ammo drum holding 180 rounds (30 bursts) can be substituted, weighing an additional 30 pounds (13.6 kg). The E-Clip fires 960 rounds (160 bursts) before it needs replacing.', 'One at a time or in bursts; each counts as one melee action, but the burst is less controlled and less accurate', NULL, NULL, NULL, 'Also known as the "Cactus Juicer" - shot at a cactus for target practice, all it leaves behind is juice where the cactus once stood. A slightly heavier version of the Big Bear 5000 firing flechette rounds instead of explosive ones, extremely popular among cyborgs and power armour pilots, who typically use it with the backpack ammo-drum. NO knock down feature. The weight includes the E-Clip power supply and a standard 42 round drum. Reloading takes one melee round (15 seconds), or 30 without the W.P. heavy weapons skill. A P.S. of 20 or higher is needed to use it without penalty, otherwise -3 to strike. Bonuses: laser targeting standard, +1 to strike on aimed shots.', 'Rifts World Book 14: New West p.176'),
('bandit-6000-grenade-launcher', 'Bandit 6000 Grenade Launcher', 'rifts', 'weapon', 40, 80000, '80,000 to 100,000 credits for the gun, 500 credits per grenade. Fair to poor availability, and the weapon is outlawed in the Coalition States.', '2D6 M.D. per single grenade or 4D6 M.D. per rapid-fire burst of two, to everything in a 12 foot (3.6 m) radius', 1, '2000 feet (610 m)', '12 in the gun; an additional 50 grenades are packed into the ammo-drum. Reloading 12 grenades by hand takes one melee round (15 seconds), or one melee action to load two.', 'One at a time, or two simultaneous at the same target; either counts as one melee action', NULL, NULL, NULL, 'Also known as the "Big Bang" assault rifle - a rapid-fire grenade launcher shaped somewhat like the Bandito Arms rail guns, and like them based on technology uncovered at Area 51, presumed to be a forgotten US Army or Air Force design originally intended for the SAMAS. The drum canister holds the main payload of 50 grenades and a folding bi-pod stand at the front supports prone fire. The gun weighs 40 lbs (18 kg) and the grenade drum another 20 lbs (9 kg); it can be used without the drum, hand loading the grenades. Designed for power armour pilots, Juicers, Crazies and cyborgs: a P.S. of 24 or higher is needed to use it without penalty, otherwise -4 to strike. Bonuses: laser targeting and telescopic scope optional, 6000 credits. The book prints the price as "80,000-100.000"; the period is a typesetting fault for a comma.', 'Rifts World Book 14: New West p.176'),
('the-bandito-light-body-armor', 'The Bandito (light body armor)', 'rifts', 'armor', 12, 10000, '10,000 credits; good to excellent availability', NULL, 0, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 38, 'A very light suit from Bandito Arms designed to be worn with power armour or used by vehicle crews, combining lightweight plates with M.D.C. padded armour. Similar in style to the Huntsman padded armour, only a little more form fitting and flexible; very popular among bandits, and with cowboys and anybody who rides a horse or pilots a light vehicle. M.D.C. by location: main body 38, head/helmet 30, arms 18 each, legs 24 each. Excellent mobility, no movement penalties. NOTE: this is not full environmental armour and has no cooling system.', 'Rifts World Book 14: New West p.177-178'),
('branaghan-armor', 'Branaghan Armor', 'rifts', 'armor', 15, 38000, '38,000 credits for the main armor, +12,000 for the overcoat or for the coat alone. Excellent availability; the overcoat is pricey because it is in such high demand.', NULL, 0, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 75, 'Named after "Jessie Branaghan", an infamous outlaw for whom the suit was custom designed. A two piece unit: a medium-heavy Bushman style suit of environmental plate body armour, and a light augmenting armoured overcoat. The helmet is light and snug with a removable face plate, and many wear the armour without it. The overcoat or long-coat - a duster - is a favourite among cowboys, gunfighters and sheriffs, being stylish, waterproof, and good for hiding a shotgun or rifle under; it is lined with lightweight mega-damage padding with plates over the shoulders and chest. Main armour 15 lbs (6.8 kg), overcoat 6 lbs (2.7 kg). M.D.C. by location: main body 75 (+28 with the overcoat), head/helmet 40, arms 28 each (+8 with the overcoat), legs 38 each (+12 with the overcoat). Mobility: fair in the heavy plate armour, -10% to climb and -20% to prowl, swim, perform acrobatics and similar; another -5% to each with the overcoat worn over it. The overcoat worn alone, as is popular among outlaws, cowboys, gunslingers and saddle tramps, costs only -5%, and -10% to swim.', 'Rifts World Book 14: New West p.178'),
('ng-maverick-riding-armor', 'NG "Maverick" Riding Armor', 'rifts', 'armor', 10, 14000, '14,000 credits; good to excellent availability', NULL, 0, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 36, 'A light Northern Gun body armour designed specifically for cowboys and other horsemen. The entire body, arms and legs are covered in light padded armour, with light polycarbonate and ceramic plates protecting the shoulders, chest, forearms, thighs and lower legs, the latter usually concealed by the leather leggings or "chaps" that come standard. It comes with an M.D.C. cowboy hat, felt or leather, with a mega-damage polycarbonate cap section; a full helmet, typically Bushman or Vaqueros, is optional for an extra 6000 credits at 35 or 45 M.D.C. respectively. M.D.C. by location: main body 36, head/hat 10 (optional helmet 35), arms 12 each, legs 16 each. Excellent mobility, no movement penalties. Extremely popular among cowboys, highwaymen, saddle tramps and gunmen. NOTE: this is not full environmental armour and has no cooling system.', 'Rifts World Book 14: New West p.179'),
('mi-vaqueros-armor', 'MI "Vaqueros" Armor', 'rifts', 'armor', 20, 40000, '40,000 credits; good to excellent availability', NULL, 0, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 90, 'A heavy environmental combat armour with a Mexican or Spanish styling, produced by the Manistique Imperium. The helmet comes with a light mesh covering for the lower face to give it an exotic cowboy or bandit look. The boots are designed with pockets that can hold a survival knife, blackjack, small to medium sized revolver or pistol, or a personal item such as chewing tobacco, a cigarette lighter or playing cards; one per boot. It comes standard with a pair of holsters and a gun belt. M.D.C. by location: main body 90, head/helmet 45, arms 32 each, legs 45 each. Poor mobility: -20% to climb, prowl, swim, or perform acrobatics and similar physical skills. The book sets the maker''s initials as "Ml" in its text layer; MI is the Manistique Imperium, which the entry names in its own opening line.', 'Rifts World Book 14: New West p.179'),
('ng-range-rider-riding-armor', 'NG "Range Rider" Riding Armor', 'rifts', 'armor', 10, 15000, '15,000 credits, a bit higher priced than the Maverick because one is paying for style; good to excellent availability', NULL, 0, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 30, 'Another light Northern Gun body armour designed with western females and riders in mind. Like the Maverick the entire body, arms and legs are covered in light padded armour, with the lower body designed as "pants" for greater manoeuvrability on horseback. For a touch of the feminine a leather skirt, opened in the front, hangs from the waist, and the upper body is tapered and fitted to show the waist and bosom. The upper chest and shoulders are covered by light polycarbonate and ceramic plates, with reinforced ceramic scale plates to protect the abdomen. The boots are reinforced with mega-damage plating protecting the lower legs and knees, and concealed plates also protect the thighs. It comes standard with an M.D.C. cowboy hat, felt or leather, with a mega-damage polycarbonate cap section; a full helmet, typically Bushman or Vaqueros, is optional for an extra 6000 credits at 35 or 45 M.D.C. respectively. M.D.C. by location: main body 30, head/hat 10 (optional helmet 35), arms 12 each, legs 15 each. Excellent mobility, no movement penalties. Extremely popular. NOTE: this is not full environmental armour and has no cooling system.', 'Rifts World Book 14: New West p.179-180'),
('ng-buffalo-riding-armor', 'NG "Buffalo" Riding Armor', 'rifts', 'armor', 18, 32000, '32,000 credits; good to excellent availability', NULL, 0, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 65, 'A heavy environmental Northern Gun body armour designed specifically with gunmen and adventurers - and bandits - in mind. It has a padded groin area with a front plate to protect the privates, which makes for easy and comfortable horseback riding. The entire upper body, abdomen, chest and shoulders are covered in heavy plates, the forearms are protected by light polycarbonate vambraces imitating a "wrapped" rawhide look, the lower legs are covered with heavy padded armour, and small concealed thigh plates sit underneath Indian style rawhide pants. It gets its name from the helmet, which has large round tinted lenses for seeing rather than a visor, and a big shaggy black mane like a buffalo; the lower mouth and chin portion can be removed and replaced as desired. M.D.C. by location: main body 65, head/helmet 40, arms 30 each, legs 28 each. Fair to good mobility: -5% to climb and -10% to prowl, swim, acrobatics and similar. Extremely popular among bandits, highwaymen, saddle tramps and adventurers.', 'Rifts World Book 14: New West p.180-181'),
('cavalry-armor-barding', 'Cavalry Armor (Barding)', 'rifts', 'armor', 30, 20000, '20,000 credits; good availability from Bandito Arms', NULL, 0, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 90, 'Light body armour FOR A HORSE - effectively high-tech "barding", made like the human suits from lightweight polycarbonates and ceramics that are tougher than steel. Fits most horses from 14 to 16 hands tall. It comes with padded leggings with plating for the upper leg, but these can be removed to leave the legs uncovered, since the legs of a horse are difficult targets requiring a called shot at -4 to strike. The pieces covering most of the leg fold around it and attach at the back and top with Velcro or laces. The thigh and upper leg is covered in light M.D.C. plates, as is the chest. M.D.C. by location: main body 90, head 50, front legs 18 each, hind legs 25 each. Very good mobility, no movement penalties without the armoured leggings; reduce speed by 5% with them. NOTE: cavalry armour is not an environmental suit, so the animal is not protected from toxic fumes, gases or radiation.', 'Rifts World Book 14: New West p.181');

-- Read the result back rather than trusting the exit code.
SELECT count(*) AS bandito_weapons FROM gear WHERE source_book LIKE 'Rifts World Book 14: New West%' AND category = 'weapon';
SELECT count(*) AS western_armor FROM gear WHERE source_book LIKE 'Rifts World Book 14: New West%' AND category = 'armor';

-- Records this run. See db/migrations/024-data-script-runs.sql.
INSERT INTO data_script_runs (filename) VALUES ('add-new-west-gear-a-bandito.sql');
